Ah well, problem solved.  Here's the story for those who like to read:

I went to my STASH and used up both Bags of Tricks to try for Stormy
and some scrolls of teleport.  I didn't get either but then the Wizard
appeared.  I was able to kill him and get back the Bell of Opening.  I
got an Amulet but it was fake. :(

So I went back to Asmodeus's Lair and found the other Wizard.  I
punched for awhile and then he disappeared.  I didn't hear him read a
scroll of teleport and I was blind so I didn't know where he went.  A
few turns later some monsters appeared, including a cockatrice.  I got
a corpse finally and started killing everything.  One level down I
found the Wizard and got back the Candle, Book, the Real Amulet, and
the Eyes of the Overworld.  Yay!

I charged back up and made it to VotD.  Then I made it to Earth without
seeing the Wizard.  Earth went by fast and so did Air.  On Fire I
encountered an Archon, which I tamed and brought with me through Water
to Astral.

On Astral a master lich and arch lich attacked right away and summoned
a bunch of monsters.  Both of my pets died in the ensuing chaos so I
put on my ring of conflict.  Pesty was left, Famine was middle, Death
was right.  I went left because I had 5 blessed potions of healing just
for Pesty.  Before I did that I switched out my +4 low boots for +1
jumping boots.  This turned out to be a very wise decision later.

In the left wing I got mobbed by Pesty and not one but TWO archons.  In
between all the Illness, Stunning, and quaffing of B!oH while getting
smacked around I died once before I teleported away both Archons.
Pesty sort of went off by himself I suppose.  Anyway, he wasn't
bothering me so that was really good.

I jumped to the altar and it was ... Neutral.  Bah!  I killed a Rogue
NPC and got some food rations for Famine.

I managed to avoid Pesty with jumping and got to center.  Here I let a
Priest NPC block the doorway and get killed by various monsters.  I
jumped past them and avoided Famine entirely.  This altar was ...
Lawful.  Doh!  Guess I have to face Death after all.  I was hoping not
because I didn't have anything to kill him with.

On the way out I got caught by Famine who made me really hungry but I
still managed to kill him.  It's a good thing I grabbed those food
rations before, though.  And martial arts really sucks.

I jumped right with Famine chasing me and me freaking out at the
computer.  "Oh crap, he's gonna catch me!"  (Does Famine even have a
gender?)

On the right side I used my last 2 teleportation charges to make a lane
(I wasn't hasted so I needed another turn) and jumped past Death.  At
the area around the temple I was mobbed by Angels and I saw an Archon
in the temple waiting for me.  Oh no!

When I jumped into the Temple I had a heck of a time finding the altar.
 There were iron chains all over the place from some fight.  Then a
bunch of monsters appeared and I couldn't move anyway.

I think the Eyes of the Overworld saved me here because otherwise that
Archon would stunned me until I was dead.  As it was I was at 50%
health from fighting Famine.

But I did manage to find the altar under some chains and viola! ......

Joeb, chaotic female human Monk




